{{> pagehead title="WildPortal - Admin" badge="SSTI"}}

  <div class="welcome">
    <h1>Admin area</h1>
    <p>Signed in as <b>{{user.name}}</b> ({{user.role}}). Manage the portal from
    the menu below.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="vk-section">
    <div class="vk-eyebrow">Admin menu</div>
    <ul class="menu">
      <li><a href="/admin">Dashboard</a></li>
      <li><a href="/admin">Users</a></li>
      <li><a href="/admin">Content</a></li>
      <li><a href="/admin">Settings</a></li>
      <li><button id="edit-template-btn" type="button">Edit Page Template</button></li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <div class="alert alert--warning">
    <div>
      <div class="alert__title">Edit Page Template</div>
      <div class="alert__body">
        The <b>Edit Page Template</b> button opens a small editor in a new window.
        Whatever you type there is compiled and rendered on the server with the
        Handlebars engine, so administrators can tweak how pages look. That server
        side compilation of your input is the vulnerability this lab teaches.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <ul class="menu" style="margin-top:14px;">
    <li><a href="/">&larr; Back to the front page</a></li>
  </ul>

<script>
  // Open the vulnerable template editor in a separate popup window, as specified
  // by the lab design (the third page opens from the admin "Edit Page Template"
  // button).
  document.getElementById("edit-template-btn").addEventListener("click", function () {
    window.open(
      "/admin/edit-template",
      "wwa_edit_template",
      "width=780,height=720,menubar=no,toolbar=no,location=no,status=no"
    );
  });
</script>
{{> pagefoot}}
